import mundane definition stdlib/divisibility/even
import mundane theorem    stdlib/divisibility/even-or-odd
import mundane definition stdlib/divisibility/odd

theorem quadratic-plus-four-even
  note        An integer is even or odd. If n = 2k, then n² + 3n + 4 is
              4k² + 6k + 4, twice 2k² + 3k + 2. If n = 2k + 1, it is
              4k² + 10k + 8, twice 2k² + 5k + 4.
  let n ∈ ℤ                                                           (H1)
  then n² + 3n + 4 is even

1.  n is even or n is odd
    mun:even-or-odd

2.  n² + 3n + 4 is even
    cases, from 1

    case
    assume n is even                                                  (C1)

    2.1.  k ∈ ℤ. n = 2k.
          obtain k: mun:even, from C1

    2.2.  n² + 3n + 4 = (2k)² + 3(2k) + 4
          substitute n = 2k (line 2.1)

    2.3.  (2k)² + 3(2k) + 4 = 2(2k² + 3k + 2)
          algebra

    2.4.  n² + 3n + 4 = 2(2k² + 3k + 2)
          calculation
            n² + 3n + 4 = (2k)² + 3(2k) + 4   2.2
                        = 2(2k² + 3k + 2)     2.3

    2.5.  n² + 3n + 4 is even
          mun:even n := n² + 3n + 4, from 2.4

    case
    assume n is odd                                                   (C2)

    2.6.  k ∈ ℤ. n = 2k + 1.
          obtain k: mun:odd, from C2

    2.7.  n² + 3n + 4 = (2k + 1)² + 3(2k + 1) + 4
          substitute n = 2k + 1 (line 2.6)

    2.8.  (2k + 1)² + 3(2k + 1) + 4 = 2(2k² + 5k + 4)
          algebra

    2.9.  n² + 3n + 4 = 2(2k² + 5k + 4)
          calculation
            n² + 3n + 4 = (2k + 1)² + 3(2k + 1) + 4   2.7
                        = 2(2k² + 5k + 4)             2.8

    2.10. n² + 3n + 4 is even
          mun:even n := n² + 3n + 4, from 2.9
